I tried the change against a local server that always answers 401, with a fresh HOME and no API keys in the environment:
• `--provider openai --api-key dummy`: the hint now says "The key passed with --api-key was rejected by the API — check the key value." It no longer says "OPENAI_API_KEY is not set" or tells the user to export it.
• `--provider google` with `GEMINI_API_KEY` set: the hint names GEMINI_API_KEY instead of the main variable name (GOOGLE_API_KEY).

What the diff does:
• Where the source is recorded: cli::parse_model_config, where the key is actually chosen, so main.rs is untouched. The alias names come from the existing providers::find_provider_key / provider_api_key_vars helpers rather than a second hand-written list.
• Tests: the wording comes from one function, auth_failure_message, which takes the source as an argument. Its tests in the new src/prompt_retry_auth_tests.rs compare the full message for each source. The "no key" and "provider's own variable" messages are checked to be exactly the old text. There is also a check that the --api-key message never contains "is not set".
• Loose ends: every new definition is used in this diff. The file-size limits in tests/module_size.rs were raised for both changed files, and ARCHITECTURE.md records the change.
• Docs: common-issues.md doesn't quote the old 401 wording, so it needed no edit.

One trade-off is written down in ARCHITECTURE.md rather than hidden: the source isn't recorded during tests, so no automated test covers the recording itself. The live runs above are the only evidence that part works. The setup-wizard part of #1062 is still open, as the task intended.

